export const principles = "=== 00-README-cheat-sheet.md ===\n# Thumbnail Playbook: Runrun Político / Noticias BQ\n\nEverything YT Packaging knows and applies when it briefs or writes a prompt for a thumbnail. Compiled 13 Nov 2026 for Derrick Serna.\n\nWhere it comes from: Derrick's soul.md (YT Packaging), the packaging skill and its references, Derrick's corrections of 8 to 10 Nov 2026, the reference page in Actions2.5 (Hollman Morris) and the 1of10 / NexLev / YouTube course notes, which are biased by the tools those vendors sell.\n\n## Files\n| # | File | What it covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| 00 | README-cheat-sheet | This page: the one-screen version |\n| 01 | principles | How to think about a thumbnail: title + thumbnail pair, one lever, cover test |\n| 02 | visual-rules-dos-donts | Fonts, subject, lighting, color, composition: dos and don'ts |\n| 03 | house-style-prompt-template | The house prompt for image generation, with slots, menus and fill rules |\n| 04 | thumbnail-text-bank-es | Spanish 2-4 word text formulas, ★ = political fit |\n| 05 | legal-and-accuracy | What text can and cannot claim about a named person |\n| 06 | qa-checklist | The checks to run before a thumbnail ships |\n| 07 | repackaging-stalled-videos | When and how to change a thumbnail after publishing |\n| 08 | worked-examples | Real prompts from Actions2.5, with the reasoning behind each |\n| 09 | title-pairing-rules | Title rules the thumbnail has to fit with |\n| 10 | sources-conflicts-open-questions | Where the sources disagree, and what is still untested |\n\n## The one-screen version\n1. **The thumbnail never repeats the title.** The title says *what*. The thumbnail adds tension or opens a *new question*. (Title \"Petro dejó perder los Panamericanos…\" → thumbnail \"¿QUIÉN NO PAGÓ?\", not \"PETRO PERDIÓ\".)\n2. **One idea, one focal point, 2-3 elements max:** subject + text + one optional supporting object, kept faint.\n3. **Text: 2-4 words, ALL CAPS, two lines.** Line 1 in yellow (#FFD700), line 2 in white, bold condensed sans with a thick black outline. Red only on ¿ and ?.\n4. **A real face with a readable emotion,** large, cut out, rim-lit, on one third of the frame. The text goes in the open space on the opposite side.\n5. **House look:** documentary style, teal↔orange gradient (#008080 / #FF6600), strong vignette, harsh side light, light grain, red play button top-left, no date, no logo, no extra text.\n6. **Pull ONE lever:** MIEDO, INTRIGA or DESEO. Name it before you write.\n7. **Cover test:** the thumbnail must work with no title, and the title with no thumbnail.\n8. **Legal:** ESTAFA / MINTIERON / ROBO about a named person only if the script backs it. Otherwise turn it into a question (\"¿?\"), attribute it, or point at the fact rather than the person.\n9. **Never promise what the video doesn't deliver.** The first 5 seconds of the video must confirm the thumbnail's promise.\n10. **Prompt in English, image text in Spanish.** Spell the image text exactly, with accents and ¿¡.\n11. **Three thumbnails per video,** one per title (main + 2 alternates). Each makes a *different* promise, not a rewording.\n12. **Grayscale + mobile test:** shrink it to phone size and convert to grey. The face and the text must still win.\n\n=== 01-principles.md ===\n# 01 · Principles: how to think before you prompt\n\n## Start from the script, never from a blank page\n- Find the **grievance**: the fact or contradiction the viewer (Colombian critics of petrismo) already feels in their gut.\n- Find the **payoff** the video actually delivers. The title names *what*; the video delivers *why*; the thumbnail adds the *tension* in between.\n- **Anchor + bet:** an anchor the viewer recognises in under a second (a known politician's face, an event, a place) plus ONE bet that creates tension. Two or three ingredients at most.\n- Before anything else, state the video in 10 words or fewer. If you can't, the concept isn't clear yet. Refocus before you write a prompt.\n\n## Title and thumbnail are a pair, not twins\n- They must **reinforce the same promise** and never contradict each other.\n- The thumbnail **never restates the title.** The title gives context; the thumbnail creates tension and opens a new question.\n  - Canonical example: title \"Why Nokia Lost the Smartphone War\" + a Nokia next to an iPhone with \"THEY SAW IT COMING\", not \"NOKIA FAILED\".\n  - House examples: title about Petro attacking Char → \"¿Y QUÉ HIZO ÉL?\"; title about Hollman Morris's case being archived → \"¿ARCHIVADO DOS VECES?\"; title about petrismo attacking Abelardo's beret → \"¿Y SUS BANDERAS?\".\n- The thumbnail carries the same **entity + conflict** as the title, through the face, the object or the text.\n\n## One emotional lever per package\nName it before you write:\n- **MIEDO** (fear): what's being lost, what's coming, what threatens the viewer. Text such as ESTO ES GRAVE, SE VIENE EL FINAL, ¿ESTAMOS JODIDOS?\n- **INTRIGA** (intrigue): something hidden, contradictory or unexplained. NO CUADRA, LO ESCONDIERON, ÉL SABÍA, ¿QUIÉN NO PAGÓ?\n- **DESEO** (desire): a win, the rival's defeat, justice, being proven right. OBRAS, NO ODIO, JUGADA MAESTRA, HUNDIDO.\nThe face's expression must match the lever: evasive or guilty for intrigue, tense or worried for fear, confident or proud for desire.\n\n## Cover test\n- The thumbnail alone, with no title, must make sense and make someone want to click.\n- The title alone, with no thumbnail, must make sense too.\n- If the thumbnail only works once you've read the title, it's a caption, not a thumbnail.\n\n## Write for the right viewer\nPetrismo critics in Colombia are the audience. Let the wrong viewer scroll past. Don't soften the package to please everyone, and don't overreach beyond what the script says (see 05).\n\n## Three thumbnails, three promises\nEach video gets three prompts: **Recomendado** (paired with the main title) plus one for each of the two alternate titles. They must be three *different* angles, not three versions of the same text. That's what makes Test & Compare useful.\n\n## Fit the channel, not the theory\nThe YouTube course, 1of10 and NexLev are direction, not law. They sell outlier tools and contradict each other on text length, numbers and so on (see 10). The channel's own results come first: when Derrick edits a page, his edits beat every rule here.\n\n=== 02-visual-rules-dos-donts.md ===\n# 02 · Visual rules: dos and don'ts\n\nSource: soul.md, \"Universal Thumbnail Principles\". These are the repeatable behaviours behind high-CTR thumbnails: readable in the feed, a click decided in under a second.\n\n## Universal\n- One clear idea and one dominant focal point. Viewers decide in under a second.\n- The thumbnail and the title reinforce the same promise.\n- High contrast (luminance + colour) is non-negotiable.\n- 2-3 elements at most: subject + text + optional supporting object.\n\n## Fonts and text\n**Do**\n- Bold, condensed, high-impact sans: Anton, Bebas Neue, Impact or similar.\n- 1-4 words (house practice: 2-4, split over two lines).\n- Big enough to read at mobile size.\n- Contrast against the background of about 4.5:1 or more.\n- Put the text in negative space or over a high-contrast area.\n- ALL CAPS (house style), or mixed case only if it stays instantly readable.\n\n**Don't**\n- Thin, script or decorative fonts.\n- More than one short phrase.\n- Text over busy areas or areas of a similar colour.\n- Small text that disappears when the image shrinks.\n- Low-contrast pairs (light grey on white, dark blue on black).\n\n## Subject, emotion and composition\n**Do**\n- A clear face with a readable emotion (surprise, anger, joy, shock, worry) when a person is involved.\n- A large subject as the clear focal point.\n- A clean cut-out or isolation when it adds clarity.\n- Rule of thirds or a strong visual hierarchy.\n- A subtle rim light or edge definition so the subject separates from the background.\n- Clean, high-contrast facial features: eyes, mouth and expression must read at small size.\n\n**Don't**\n- Tiny faces or several faces competing.\n- A subject flat against a background of a similar tone.\n- Faces over-edited into something uncanny or heavily filtered that loses the emotion.\n- Secondary objects that clutter the frame and dilute the subject.\n- A neutral or unreadable expression when emotion is the hook.\n\n## Lighting, contrast, highlights\n**Do**\n- High overall contrast: bright highlights, deep shadows.\n- A rim or edge light to separate the subject.\n- More local contrast on the face and the key elements.\n- The brightest point pulls the eye to the subject or the text.\n- **Grayscale test:** the hierarchy must still be obvious in grey.\n\n**Don't**\n- Flat, even light with no separation.\n- A background that competes in brightness with the subject.\n- Shadows so crushed that facial detail is lost.\n- Subtle gradients that vanish at small size.\n\n## Colour and palettes\n**Do**\n- Complementary or warm-on-cool pairs: yellow/black, red/yellow, blue/orange, yellow/purple. House pair: teal/orange.\n- A limited palette of 2-3 dominant colours.\n- High-contrast text: yellow or white on dark, black or dark on light.\n- Saturated colour used for emphasis, not everywhere.\n- Colour contrast that still works in grayscale.\n\n**Don't**\n- Low-contrast pairs (red on green, blue on purple, similar mid-tones).\n- Lots of colours competing.\n- Muted or desaturated palettes that melt into the YouTube feed.\n- Text in a colour with low contrast against what's behind it.\n\n## Repeatable workflow (6 steps)\n1. Define the single idea the thumbnail has to say.\n2. Choose and isolate the main subject (a face whenever it's relevant).\n3. Apply strong separation: rim light, cut-out or contrast.\n4. Add 1-4 words of bold, high-contrast text if needed.\n5. Limit the palette to 2-3 high-contrast colours.\n6. Confirm it matches the title's promise without repeating it.\n\n=== 03-house-style-prompt-template.md ===\n# 03 · House prompt template (Runrun Político / Noticias BQ)\n\nThe style is locked to the Actions2.5 reference page (Hollman Morris): documentary look, teal↔orange gradient, the real photo of the subject as focal point, two lines of ALL CAPS text in yellow + white, red only on ¿ ?, small play button top-left, no date, no logo.\n\n- **The prompt is written in English.** The text inside the image stays in **Spanish**, spelled exactly (accents, ¿ ¡, commas).\n- The prompt always assumes a **reference photo of the real person is attached** (\"the attached man/woman… faithful to reference image\"). Never ask the model to invent a politician's face.\n\n## Brief block (what goes on the Notion page)\n```\n### Recomendado · [THUMBNAIL TEXT or short concept]        ← pairs with the main title\n### Promesa: [promise in a few words] · [alternate title]  ← one per alternate\nSujeto: [Person], usa una foto de [Person]\n[code block with the English prompt]\n```\n\n## Template\n```txt\nDocumentary-style YouTube thumbnail. {GRADIENT} with a strong vignette. The subject is the attached {man/woman}, {FULL NAME}, cutout against the gradient, tight head-and-shoulders, positioned on the {left/right} side of frame, facing {right/left}, {EXPRESSION}, faithful to reference image. High contrast, harsh side light, slight rim light separating subject from background, sharp focus, light grain. Faint, heavily blurred background element showing {ONE CONTEXT OBJECT}. Text overlay in bold condensed sans-serif ALL CAPS with thick black outline (2-3px) and drop shadow, very large, positioned center-{right/left} in clean open space, spanning 45% of frame width. Top line reads \"{LINE 1}\" in bright yellow (#FFD700). Bottom line reads \"{LINE 2}\" in white. {RED RULE}. YouTube play button (red, white triangle) in top-left corner. No date. No channel logo. No text other than the two lines. Documentary aesthetic with {MOOD 1}, {MOOD 2}, high contrast.\n```\n\n## Slot rules\n| Slot | Rule | Options |\n|---|---|---|\n| GRADIENT | Alternate between the 3 thumbnails of a video so they look different in Test & Compare | A: \"Dark teal-to-orange gradient background (#008080 to #FF6600)\" · B: \"Orange-to-teal gradient background (warm orange #FF6600 to deep teal #008080)\" |\n| Side | Subject on one third, text in the open space on the other. Alternate it between variants too | Subject left, facing right → text center-right · Subject right, facing left → text center-left |\n| EXPRESSION | Must match the lever and stay faithful to the person | Intrigue: evasive, looking slightly away / guarded / suspicious · Fear: tense / worried / somber · Conflict: angry, mid-speech / defiant · Desire: confident, proud half-smile / triumphant |\n| CONTEXT OBJECT | ONE object, faint and heavily blurred. It supports the subject and never competes with it. Concrete and visual | case file folder with Fiscalía seal, courtroom gavel, wall calendar page, stadium at night with floodlights, unlit torch cauldron in empty stadium, city skyline, M-19 flag, Congress chamber, ballot box, stacks of cash, prison bars |\n| LINE 1 / LINE 2 | 2-4 words in total, from the text bank (04). Line 1 carries the hook word. A question splits over the two lines (\"¿QUIÉN NO\" / \"PAGÓ?\") | See 04 |\n| RED RULE | If the text has ¿ ?: `Red only on the \"¿\" and \"?\".` · If not: `No red text.` | Red is never used on a whole word |\n| MOOD | 2 adjectives that match the lever | investigative, somber, accusatory, judicial, tense, confrontational, political, triumphant, civic pride |\n\n## Hard constraints to keep in every prompt\n- \"No date. No channel logo. No text other than the two lines.\"\n- Never two faces competing. If the story is a contrast between two people (Petro vs Char), choose ONE face per thumbnail and let the other side live in the object or the text. A split-screen with two faces is only an exception, for a test, and both faces must stay large.\n- Don't distort or caricature the real person (no fake tears, no handcuffs or prison clothes on someone who hasn't been convicted). The expression comes from a real photo.\n- No symbols, uniforms or objects that imply a crime the script doesn't support (see 05).\n\n## Pre-send prompt check\n- [ ] The image text is spelled exactly in Spanish, with accents and ¿¡\n- [ ] 2-4 words, two lines, yellow on top / white below\n- [ ] The red rule matches the text (questions only)\n- [ ] One face, one faint object, nothing else\n- [ ] Gradient and side alternate across the 3 variants\n- [ ] The expression matches the lever\n- [ ] The text doesn't repeat the title it's paired with\n\n=== 04-thumbnail-text-bank-es.md ===\n# Banco de textos para miniatura (español, Colombia)\n\nAdaptado por Derrick Serna (2026-11-10) desde un banco en inglés. No es traducción literal: está en el registro colombiano de Runrun Político / Noticias BQ.\n\nCómo usarlo:\n- Punto de partida, no plantilla: elige la fórmula que abra una pregunta NUEVA respecto al título (regla de Miniaturas del SKILL). 2-4 palabras, MAYÚSCULAS.\n- [X] = actor, partido, entidad o tema del guion (PETRO, EL PACTO, LA REFORMA, ECOPETROL...).\n- ★ = encaja muy bien en política/noticias. ○ = solo si el guion lo pide. Las secciones de dinero, tiempo y superación casi nunca aplican.\n- Riesgo legal: ESTAFA, MINTIERON, FALSO, ROBO, etc. sobre una persona nombrada solo si el guion lo sostiene; si no, usa \"¿?\", atribuye (\"DICE LA FISCALÍA\") o apunta al hecho, no a la persona. Nada de groserías explícitas (\"JODIDOS\" sí; nada peor).\n\n## 11. Alarma y advertencia\n★ ESTO ES GRAVE / ESTO DA MIEDO · ★ SE ACABÓ / SE ACABÓ [X] · ○ NO VAYA AHÍ / ALÉJESE · ★ [X] ENLOQUECIÓ · ★ ESTO NO ES NORMAL · ★ ESTAFA / LO ESTÁN ESTAFANDO · ○ [X] ESTÁ MUERTO · ★ ESTO NO DEBERÍA EXISTIR / DEBERÍA SER ILEGAL / ¿CÓMO ES ESTO LEGAL? · ★ FALSO / 90% FALSO / TODO ES MENTIRA / NOS ESTÁN MINTIENDO · ★ ¿EL FIN DE [X]? / SE VIENE EL FINAL · ★ ESTAMOS JODIDOS / ¿ESTAMOS JODIDOS? · ★ PROHIBIDO\n\n## 12. Misterio e información oculta\n★ ¿POR QUÉ [X] ESTÁ EN TODAS PARTES? · ★ NADIE LE CUENTA ESTO / NADIE SABE ESTO · ★ LO QUE NO SE VE · ○ ¿TESORO ESCONDIDO? · ★ OCULTO / LO ESCONDIERON · ★ LA VERDAD · ★ EL SECRETO · ★ NO CUADRA / ESTO NO TIENE SENTIDO / NADIE LO EXPLICA · ○ NO LE CUENTE A NADIE / NUNCA LE DICEN ESTO · ★ SEÑALES DE [X]\n\n## 13. Historia y drama\n★ MINTIERON / MINTIERON SOBRE [X] · ★ ÉL SABÍA / ELLOS SABÍAN · ★ ¡¿QUÉ PASÓ?! / ESTO FUE LO QUE PASÓ · ★ ASÍ EMPEZÓ / YA EMPEZÓ / ESTÁ EMPEZANDO · ★ YA ESTÁ PASANDO / ALGO SE VIENE · ★ EL ERROR / UN ERROR FATAL / EL MISMO ERROR · ★ NOS EQUIVOCAMOS / ¿QUÉ SALIÓ MAL? · ★ \"[CITA TEXTUAL DEL PROTAGONISTA]\" (muy fuerte en política: frase real del guion, entre comillas) · ○ ¡¿Y ESE QUIÉN ES?!\n\n## 14. Órdenes\n○ EMPIECE YA / EMPIECE AQUÍ · ○ HAGA ESTO / HAGA ESTO PRIMERO · ★ NUNCA [X] · ★ PAREN [X] / DEJEN DE HACER ESTO · ○ CÓPIEME · ○ ¡BÓTELO YA!\n\n## 15. Superación personal (casi nunca aplica)\nLA REGLA DE [X] / LA REGLA DEL [X]% · APRENDA LO QUE SEA · EL ARTE DE [X] · EL TRUCO / ATAJO · VENTAJAS INJUSTAS · TODAVÍA ESTÁ A TIEMPO / NO ES TARDE · OJALÁ LO HUBIERA SABIDO ANTES · CURSO COMPLETO / GUÍA COMPLETA · ★ SE LO EXPLICO (útil para videos explicativos) · ES MUY FÁCIL · EL PLAN\n\n## 16. Dinero y resultados\n○ $0 → $[X] · ★ POBRES / RICOS (contraste, p. ej. congresistas vs. ciudadanos) · ★ $[X] AL MES / $[X] DIARIOS (sueldos, contratos) · ★ ¿VALE LA PENA? / PLATA BOTADA · ○ NO COMPRO NADA · ○ ¿QUIERE TENER UN [X]?\n\n## 17. Tiempo (casi nunca aplica)\nUNA HORA AL DÍA · DOMINE [X] EN [X] HORAS · SOLO TOMA [X] HORAS · TODO LISTO ANTES DE LAS [X]AM\n\n## 18. Comparaciones\n★ ANTES / DESPUÉS · ★ DÍA 1 / DÍA [X] (p. ej. DÍA 1 / DÍA 800 de gobierno) · ○ NOVATO → EXPERTO · ○ NIVEL 1–[X] / [X] NIVELES DE [X] · ★ INICIO / FINAL · ○ EXTINTO / VIVO · ★ REAL / FALSO · ★ MITO / REALIDAD · ○ YO (con flecha)\n\n## 19. \"Sí funciona\" (contrario)\n○ ESTO SÍ FUNCIONA / FUNCIONA DEMASIADO · ○ ABURRIDO PERO FUNCIONA · ★ PURA MATEMÁTICA / ES SIMPLE MATEMÁTICA (cifras, votos, presupuesto) · ○ RARO, PERO FUNCIONA · ★ GENIAL / JUGADA MAESTRA (estrategia política) · ★ PROBLEMA / ESTO ES UN PROBLEMA · ○ PARECE TRAMPA · ○ LOS PROBÉ TODOS · ★ SOBREVALORADO / PURO HUMO\n\n## 20. Reacciones\n○ ¿ABURRIDO? · ★ ¡NO PUEDE SER! / ¡QUÉ LOCURA! · ★ ¿QUÉ CARAJOS? / ¿QUÉ ES ESTO? · ★ ESTÁ CERCA / NI CERCA · ★ ESTO ESTÁ MAL / ESTO ES GRAVE · ○ EL MEJOR / EL GOAT · ★ SE VA A ARREPENTIR / CERO ARREPENTIMIENTO\n\n## 21. Veredictos de una palabra\n★ CANCELADO · ★ VENCIDO / SE LE ACABÓ EL TIEMPO · ★ MUERTO. / ENTERRADO. · ★ ESCALOFRIANTE / DA MIEDO · ★ DESCARADO · ★ HUNDIDO · ★ TRAICIÓN\n\n=== 05-legal-and-accuracy.md ===\n# 05 · Legal and accuracy\n\nA thumbnail is the most aggressive claim in the package and the one that gets screenshotted. Same rules as the script, applied more strictly.\n\n## Text about a named person\n- **ESTAFA, MINTIERON, FALSO, ROBO, CORRUPTO, CRIMINAL** and similar words on a named person: only if the script backs it with something proven or clearly attributed.\n- If it doesn't, use one of three exits:\n  1. **Turn it into a question:** \"¿MINTIÓ?\", \"¿ARCHIVADO DOS VECES?\", \"¿QUIÉN NO PAGÓ?\". The \"¿?\" also gets the red accent.\n  2. **Attribute it:** \"DICE LA FISCALÍA\", or a real quote from the script in quotation marks.\n  3. **Point at the fact, not the person:** \"NO CUADRA\", \"ESTO NO ES NORMAL\", \"LO ESCONDIERON\".\n- **Presumption of innocence:** if there's no conviction, the image doesn't suggest one. No handcuffs, prison bars, prison clothes or mugshot framing on someone who hasn't been convicted. A file folder, a gavel or a calendar are fine as context.\n- Quotes: only a real phrase that appears in the script. Never put words in someone's mouth.\n- No explicit swearing. \"JODIDOS\" is the ceiling.\n\n## Accuracy\n- Never promise what the recorded video doesn't deliver. If the thumbnail says \"¿QUIÉN NO PAGÓ?\", the video has to answer it.\n- Keep names, numbers and dates exactly as the script says them.\n- Don't borrow authority (\"EXPERTOS\", \"CIENTÍFICOS\") unless the script cites them.\n- Superlatives and urgency (\"LO PEOR\", \"ESCÁNDALO\") only if the script itself frames it that way.\n\n## Face and image\n- Always use a real photo of the person, faithful to the reference. Don't caricature, deform or change their features.\n- The expression can be picked (evasive, angry, proud), but it must exist in a real photo. Don't make the model fake tears or a grimace.\n- Party symbols and flags (M-19, the war-to-the-death flag) only when the script talks about them, as with the Abelardo beret video.\n\n=== 06-qa-checklist.md ===\n# 06 · QA checklist (run on each thumbnail before it ships)\n\n## Concept\n- [ ] I can state the video in ≤10 words.\n- [ ] I named the lever: MIEDO / INTRIGA / DESEO.\n- [ ] The text **doesn't repeat** the title it's paired with, or the alternates. It adds a new angle or question.\n- [ ] **Cover test:** it works with no title; the title works with no thumbnail.\n- [ ] The 3 thumbnails of the video make 3 different promises.\n- [ ] The **first 5 seconds** of the video visibly confirm the promise. If not, flag it on the page.\n\n## Text\n- [ ] 2-4 words, ALL CAPS, two lines (yellow / white).\n- [ ] Correct Spanish: accents, ¿ ¡, no typos. (The reference page has a typo in its title, \"archivadon\". Don't copy typos.)\n- [ ] It starts from a ★ formula in the bank (04), or has a reason not to.\n- [ ] Red only on ¿ ? (or \"No red text\").\n- [ ] It passes the legal check (05).\n\n## Image\n- [ ] One face, large, cut out, rim-lit, with a readable emotion that matches the lever.\n- [ ] One faint context object, at most.\n- [ ] The text sits in open space on the opposite side from the face.\n- [ ] 2-3 dominant colours; it passes the grayscale test and the phone-size test.\n- [ ] No date, no logo, no extra text.\n\n## Page (Notion, Actions2.5)\n- [ ] \"## Miniaturas\" with: Recomendado + one \"Promesa: … · [alternate title]\" per alternate.\n- [ ] Under each: \"Sujeto: [person], usa una foto de [person]\" + a code block with the prompt in English.\n- [ ] No reasoning, scores or notes on the page. It's a deliverable, not a log.\n- [ ] For Test & Compare: main title + first 2 alternates, each with its own thumbnail. Record it in the Results log.\n\n=== 07-repackaging-stalled-videos.md ===\n# 07 · Repackaging a stalled video\n\n## When to act\nOnly if impressions are still rising or holding steady **and** retention is above the channel average. In that case the video is fine and the packaging is the problem. If retention is weak, a new thumbnail won't save it.\n\nNoticias BQ baseline (28 days, 11 Oct to 7 Nov 2026): 8.6% CTR, average view duration 2:13.\n\n## Ladder (one change at a time, wait 24-48 h between steps)\n1. **Sharpen the thumbnail:** 2-4 words, a new tension, passes the cover test.\n2. Swap in an alternate title from \"Títulos alternos\".\n3. Update the wording (year, names, current framing).\n4. Tie it to a current Colombian news event, if the script supports it. This is the strongest lever for this channel.\n5. Last resort: remake the video bigger.\n\n## How to change a thumbnail\n- First, diagnose in one line which lever the current one pulls and why it isn't getting clicks.\n- **Change the lever and/or the format, not just the words.** Example: ¿INTOCABLE? (vague intrigue about the person) → NO SON LOS JUECES (intrigue that points at a hidden mechanism, a new question: then who is it?).\n- Try the two reframes:\n  - A **proven format:** ANTES / DESPUÉS, DÍA 1 / DÍA [X], MITO / REALIDAD, REAL / FALSO, or a comparison of two objects.\n  - A **question:** \"¿QUÉ TAN PELIGROSO?\", \"¿QUIÉN…?\". Avoid opening with \"¿POR QUÉ…?\".\n- If you borrow from an outlier (from the channel or a neighbour), write in one line WHY it got clicks (lever, open question, character) and carry over the mechanism, never the words. If you can't explain why it worked, don't borrow from it.\n- Every proposal to Derrick says: old lever/format → new lever/format, in one line. Derrick makes the change in Studio, then it's measured at 24-48 h.\n\n## Past cases (for reference)\n- \"Por qué Petro no va a terminar en la cárcel\": 5.5K impressions, stalled; 7.6% CTR; 46.1% viewed. Thumbnail ¿INTOCABLE? → NO SON LOS JUECES proposed (status: waiting for Derrick in Studio).\n- Timochenko, Mancuso and \"Contratos por favores s3xuales\": titles already changed with no effect (+1, 0, +12 views). Don't touch them again.\n\n=== 08-worked-examples.md ===\n# 08 · Worked examples (real prompts from Actions2.5)\n\n## A. Reference page: Hollman Morris (the style everything copies)\nTitle: \"¿Por qué archivadon dos veces el caso de Hollman Morris?\" (sic: the typo is in the original, don't copy it).\n\n**Recomendado: ¿ARCHIVADO / DOS VECES?** · Lever: INTRIGA · Object: closed file folder with the Fiscalía seal\n```txt\nDocumentary-style YouTube thumbnail. Dark teal-to-orange gradient background (#008080 to #FF6600) with a strong vignette. The subject is the attached man, Hollman Morris, cutout against the gradient, tight head-and-shoulders, positioned on the left side of frame, facing right, serious, guarded expression, faithful to reference image. High contrast, harsh side light, slight rim light separating subject from background, sharp focus, light grain. Faint, heavily blurred background element showing a closed case file folder with a Fiscalía General de la Nación seal. Text overlay in bold condensed sans-serif ALL CAPS with thick black outline (2-3px) and drop shadow, very large, positioned center-right in clean open space, spanning 45% of frame width. Top line reads \"¿ARCHIVADO\" in bright yellow (#FFD700). Bottom line reads \"DOS VECES?\" in white. Red only on the \"¿\" and \"?\". YouTube play button (red, white triangle) in top-left corner. No date. No channel logo. No text other than the two lines. Documentary aesthetic with investigative, somber, high contrast.\n```\nNote: one of the reference page's alternates uses \"¿PRESCRITO? / 17 DE NOVIEMBRE\". It breaks two house rules (a date in the image, and a second line that adds no tension). Don't copy that pattern.\n\n## B. Char vs Petro (13 Nov 2026): one contrast, three angles\nMain title: \"Petro dejó perder los Panamericanos; Char le RESPONDE con un estadio\"\n\n| Variant | Face | Expression | Text | Lever | Object | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Recomendado | Char | proud half-smile | OBRAS, / NO ODIO | DESEO | stadium at night with floodlights | The title already says the facts; the thumbnail adds the moral verdict. No ¿?, so \"No red text\". |\n| Alt 1 \"La VERDAD de cómo Petro dejó perder…\" | Petro | evasive, looking away | ¿QUIÉN NO / PAGÓ? | INTRIGA | unlit torch cauldron, empty stadium | Opens the question the title only hints at (the payment that never came). |\n| Alt 2 \"Petro ataca a Char, pero…\" | Petro | angry, mid-speech | ¿Y QUÉ / HIZO ÉL? | INTRIGA/conflict | Barranquilla skyline at dusk | Turns the attack back on him without repeating \"Panamericanos\". |\n\nGradient and side alternate (teal→orange on the left / orange→teal on the right) so the three read as different in Test & Compare.\n\n## C. Petrismo vs Abelardo's beret (13 Nov 2026)\nTitle: \"El petrismo ataca la BOINA de Abelardo y calla sobre Mancuso\" → thumbnail of Petro with **¿Y SUS BANDERAS?**\nWhy: the title already names the beret and Mancuso. The thumbnail opens the new, unmentioned angle (the M-19 flags), which is also the new topic of this video. Mancuso and the stage in Medellín had already been used in an earlier video.\n\n## Anti-examples (what not to do)\n- Title \"Petro dejó perder los Panamericanos\" + thumbnail \"PETRO PERDIÓ LOS JUEGOS\" → repeats the title, no new tension.\n- \"CORRUPTO\" over the face of someone who hasn't been convicted → legal risk. Use \"¿?\" or point at the fact.\n- Two faces small side by side, plus a logo, a date and three lines of text → fails the feed and the grayscale test.\n- A thin or script font, or yellow text over a light orange area → unreadable at phone size.\n\n=== 09-title-pairing-rules.md ===\n# 09 · Title pairing rules (the thumbnail must fit these)\n\nCopied as-is from the packaging skill. The thumbnail carries the same entity + conflict as the title and never repeats its words.\n\n# Title guidelines (Derrick's data-backed spec, applies to ALL titles)\n\nSource: TITLE-GUIDELINES-for-AI (Derrick, 2026-11-08). Spanish long-form political commentary, Colombian right-of-centre audience. Priors, not laws.\n\n## Priority\n1. Subject: named entity + conflict. 2. House formula. 3. Form (verbs, caps, length). 4. Decoration (emoji, pipes, \"?\") has no effect: don't spend time on it.\n\n## Hard rules (reject candidate if violated)\n- H1 Length 40-70 chars incl. spaces. Hard max 85.\n- H2 Exactly one named human/institutional antagonist, or one named protagonist with a conflict/exposé verb. Zero named actors = flop.\n- H3 No meta/self-referential/event subjects (host speeches, awards, courses, \"mi experiencia\").\n- H4 Never a verbatim quote as the whole title; quote fragment <= 40%.\n- H5 No digits unless the number is the hook. Default: no numbers.\n- H6 No first person (me, mi, respondo, denuncio, explico). Third person about the actors.\n- H7 1-3 ALL-CAPS words, never 0, never whole title.\n- H8 No Unicode styled letters, no leetspeak.\n- H9 No interview/guest framing as hook.\n\n## Soft scoring (add)\n- Conflict verb (+): destroza, aplasta, humilla, desenmascara, desmonta, ataca, explota, enfrenta, refuta, derrota, frena.\n- Opponent role noun (+): periodista, diputado, senador, juez, ministro, petrista, aliado, izquierdista, experto.\n- Exposé verb (+): destapa, revela, filtra, esconde, oculta, nadie, verdad, delata.\n- Urgency marker (max one, +): escándalo, urgente, grave, bomba, insólito.\n- Superlative (small +): el peor, más corrupto, de la historia.\n- Penalize: explainer framing (análisis, claves, explica), \"you\" address (tu, usted), abstract ideology noun with no human actor, leading \"¿Por qué…?\".\n- Neutral: leading emoji, brand suffix, colon/pipe, generic \"?\".\n\n## House formula (default for own channel)\n[ACTOR] + conflict/exposé verb (past tense or present) + [ACTOR/ROLE] [+ short context]. Mix of No gire a la izquierda + Julio César Iglesias: \"La DELIRANTE propuesta de Petro…\", \"ACTOR DESTROZÓ A ACTOR\".\nAvoid: macro-economics or reform explainers without a villain, foreign politics, single-actor announcements.\n\n## Entity heat (Colombia, 2026-03 to 09; recompute monthly)\nPetro x1.20, Abelardo/De La Espriella x1.12, Cepeda x1.05, Congreso x0.81, elecciones/encuestas x0.61, Paloma x0.53, Uribe x0.47. National figure as grammatical subject, secondary figure as object/context. Follow up a hit entity once; stop at first non-hit.\n\n## Emotional levers, reframes and outliers (Derrick, 2026-11-10)\n- Every title pulls ONE emotional lever, named before writing it:\n  - MIEDO (fear): what is lost, what is coming, what threatens the viewer (\"Lo que se viene con…\", \"El peligro de…\").\n  - INTRIGA (intrigue): a gap: something hidden, contradictory, unexplained (\"Lo que nadie dijo de…\", \"La verdad detrás de…\").\n  - DESEO (desire): a win, the rival's defeat, justice, being proven right (\"Así frenaron a…\", \"La jugada que tumbó…\").\n- Format reframes: when a candidate is flat, try at least one before discarding the topic:\n  1. New format: drop the topic into a format already proven (on the channel or a neighbour outlier). Example: \"$1 vs $100K katana\" → \"I tried every katana\". Political: an exposé becomes a ranking or a comparison (\"Todas las mentiras de X sobre Y\", \"X ANTES vs. X AHORA\").\n  2. Reframe as a question: \"I built the most dangerous whip\" → \"How dangerous is a whip?\". Political: \"La reforma de X es peligrosa\" → \"¿Qué tan PELIGROSA es la reforma de X?\". Keep the named actor; a leading \"¿Por qué…?\" stays penalized, so prefer \"¿Qué tan…?\", \"¿Cuánto…?\", \"¿Quién…?\", mostly in alternates.\n- Outlier rule: outlier theory only fails when used wrong. Never copy an outlier just because it is one. Before borrowing a title or thumbnail from one, write in one line WHY it got people to click (viewer psychology: which lever, which gap, which actor) and carry over that mechanism, not the words. If the reason can't be stated, don't use it.\n- Repackaging (also for stalled videos): change the lever and the frame, not just the words. Example: \"4 Hidden Habits That Hurt Your Child's Confidence\" (list, soft intrigue) → \"The Fastest Way to Kill Your Child's Confidence\" (one thing, fear, stronger verb). Political: \"Tres errores de X en la reforma\" → \"El error que puede HUNDIR la reforma de X\". Keep H5 (no digits) and H6 (no \"you\"/first person) when adapting.\n\n## Procedure\n1. Pick ONE protagonist (hottest entity) and ONE antagonist (role or person). If none: flag \"weak subject: consider re-angle\" and still proceed.\n2. Name the lever (MIEDO, INTRIGA or DESEO). Generate 8 candidates, including at least one format reframe and one question reframe; reject on H1-H9, score by soft rules.\n3. Return top 3 in the page: main title + 2 alternates, with at least one exposé framing and one conflict framing. Label alternates \"Exposé: ...\" / \"Conflicto: ...\".\n4. Thumbnail text must carry the same entity + conflict.\n5. Never overstate: titles must stay true to the script (attribution, presumption of innocence; e.g. do not say named prisoners \"operaban\" a network if the script says use is still to be established).\n6. Mention in the reply that titles should be loaded into YouTube Test & Compare (3 titles/video) and logged in the Results log.\n\n=== 10-sources-conflicts-open-questions.md ===\n# 10 · Sources, conflicts and open questions\n\n## Sources (priority order)\n1. **Derrick's edits** on final pages: they beat everything else.\n2. **soul.md · YT Packaging** (Notion): page structure, house style, universal principles.\n3. **Packaging skill** + references (title guidelines, Spanish text bank adapted by Derrick, 10 Nov 2026).\n4. **Derrick's corrections** (8-10 Nov 2026): thumbnail ≠ title, emotional levers, reframes, outlier rule.\n5. **1of10 / NexLev / the YouTube course / Niche Finder** (Derrick's notes in Notion): direction, not law. They sell outlier tools and contradict each other on title length, numbers and how much text a thumbnail should have.\n\n## Known conflicts\n| Topic | Says | Says | What the house does |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Words in the image | soul.md: 1-4 | Skill/QA: 2-4 | 2-4 split over two lines; a single word only for a one-word verdict (HUNDIDO, CANCELADO) |\n| Date in the image | soul.md: \"no date\" | The reference page has an alternate with \"17 DE NOVIEMBRE\" | No date |\n| Red | Universal principles allow red/yellow | House: red only on ¿ ? | House rule |\n| Numbers | Vendors: numbers help | Title guidelines: no digits unless the number is the hook | Same in the thumbnail: only if the number IS the story (e.g. $ of a contract) |\n| Two people | \"Don't use multiple competing faces\" | Contrast stories (Char vs Petro) invite a split-screen | One face per variant; split-screen only as a deliberate test |\n\n## Open questions (not yet tested on Noticias BQ)\n- Do questions with ¿? get more clicks than declarative verdicts (OBRAS, NO ODIO)? Measure in Test & Compare.\n- Angry face vs evasive face on Petro: which gets more CTR?\n- Does the context object add anything, or is face + text enough?\n- The teal/orange house look vs neighbour channels (El Control, Dr. Alex Law, Santiago Vélez): their thumbnails haven't been read yet.\n\nEach Test & Compare result should be logged in the Results log so these rules can be updated with the channel's own data.";
